/-
Johnson/Desc/Kinds/Law/K7AtMgAll.lean.
K7Riders' TWO FIELDS TAKE, BESIDE "reached", THE TABLE's PROMISE AT THE STATE IN FRONT
(onQ ... 338) AND AT THE STATE BEHIND (onQ ... 339). frames_mgAll, the
riders' one caller, has both in hand.
carry 23 speaks of the strings in front and behind, which agree
beneath the piece's base alone, and that the trees that the sentence reads lie beneath it is the
promise's clause on the book.


AT THE COMPOSED MEANING the
closed meaning beneath says beside a public item's test "the table First.saysNone (Johnson/Desc/First/AllSaid.lean) books that no sentence is meant here"
(Desc/Sound/MgBase.lean: pubP q := (First.saysNone q).isSome = true): at
tokenSmall the table books it ("the head's"): so k7_kindTied_mgBase hands in rfl.

WHAT IT DOES NOT SHOW. No soundness. STILL A RULE UNDER A BILL: NO MEMBER: no piece of the IOP as
written in Lean is shown to meet hall. hall ASKS, AT THE NUMBER 338: K7Rest's SIX FIELDS
(Law/K7Seated.lean: yes, front, book, told, req, tok) · A FENCE (the tenants of the two pins that
are open there sit in trees that were sent in front of the piece: x.1 < q.base) · Wp.hS = W.hS ·
K7Riders' TWO FIELDS (pile, carry: two of the eight items that ride past the place). SEVEN PREMISES
ON PARAMETERS STAY AT THE CLOSED MEANING BENEATH: hseg : headLink Wp = 24 · hhead : D.headPart is
headPartK6 · hK : D.put turns the reply alone · hplan : a test on the plan · hbase :
the reading's sentence "base" at link 24 does not read the witness's token · hsmp, hdecT : the
samples' reader D.smp and the decoder D.decT are the same at two states that agree in what the place
leaves (K7Leaves).
NO EXAMPLE SHOWS THAT hall OR ANY OF THE SEVEN CAN BE MET, TOGETHER OR ONE BY ONE, AT THE RELEASE's
VALUES: every field of D is a parameter; if a closed term of D.smp or D.decT reads where the chain
stands, the reply or the statement's groups, its premise is false. The row is a bare letter; there
is no premise on the goals' scope. The composed meaning in this form (Desc/Sound/MgAll.lean) is
the reference form (not checked here) and not the form that counts.
WORDS. "The verifier's state": the value of type S that the sub-protocols hand on. "The second
form": the chain of promises with a condition Rch beside the table's promise at every border
(Desc/Sound/TiedR.lean).
LETTERS. Under "there is", inside hall: B, Bst, W, l, name, front, tl, told: the caller's to name;
nothing in the conclusion reads them. Rch: free.
OBJECT. Desc/Sound/MgAll.lean's mgAll D Mg (at the small list of extra public tests), the
full chain's links' sorts and list of places (Desc/Sound/AtDriver.lean: linksFull; flatPlacesOf
linksFull true), and KindTiedR at the kind K7.
USER. The counted form of the next token's law: InScope, LaidAt, PlanOk, FoldFacts give KindTiedR at
the closed constant (P5J.mgAtAll, Johnson/P5J/MgAtAll.lean).
WHAT IT IS. THE NEXT TOKEN's KIND's SHARE OF THE CHAIN OF PROMISES, SECOND FORM, AT THE COMPOSED
MEANING AND THE FULL CHAIN. OF THE BILL's NINETEEN FIELDS TWELVE ARE HAD HERE (K7Table's six; dec,
order, held, shown, pub, pubP of K7State's seven), NOT FOR NOTHING: UNDER THE SEVEN PREMISES ABOVE
AND hall's fence AND Wp.hS = W.hS; THE THIRTEENTH, frames, IS CUT DOWN TO TWO RIDERS, WHICH hall
STILL ASKS; SIX STAY WHOLE IN hall.
  place338, place339, only338, open338, noRows338, sampled338, ins338, readsOpen_full,
  rowsApart_full, len338, pubFront338, pubStep338, pubTied339   the table at the border 338: the
                    kernel's evaluation.
  constr_mgAll, decIs_mgAll   the meaning's two fields that the proofs open.
  tok_terms_one     the field "tok", to the letter, at P5J/TokTerms.lean's terms (not handed in).
  tokenSmall_mgAll  the public test that the next token's row makes.
  smpHeld_withFresh "the state holds the sample" reads no group.
  K7Leaves, place_leaves, piece_leaves, place_index   what the place leaves of the verifier's state:
                    all but where the chain stands, the reply, and the statement's groups.
  K7Riders          what is left of "frames": pile and carry 23.
  pub_mgAll, pubP_mgAll, dec_mgAll, frames_mgAll   four of K7State's fields.
  state_mgAll       K7State whole.
  k7_kindTied_mgAll the statement, general in the meaning beneath, under hmore, hP, hMg on it.
  k7_kindTied_mgBase   at the closed meaning beneath: these three fall.
IN THE SECOND FORM, general
in Rch. order: "in order" is the meaning beneath's own test
and a test on the public part alone. held: smpHeld_rides
(Desc/Sound/SigRides.lean) asks that the statement stay, which is false at this place (the entry of
the head's link lays one fresh group): hence smpHeld_withFresh. shown: that file's shownJT_rides and
noCollJT_rides, under the fence and hsmp. dec: Desc/Sound/DecodesRides.lean's cell_behind, under
hdecT. pub: one item is made, one dropped, two tied ones are kept BY HAND: the kind-free
rule (Desc/First/PubFoot.lean) books them as reading the whole statement and all that goes on to the
later chains, both of which this place turns. pubP: behind the row one item is open, and the
composed meaning says nothing of its own beside its test. frames: of the ten items open at 338 two
are the row's own; of the eight riders six are paid: the committed table's pin, the two open pins (a
pin does not read the witness's token), and the head's sentence at idn, rider and small
(Law/K7Sides.lean).
NEAREST RELATIVES:
riders341_full, reads_full, apart_full and open_iff_mem (Desc/Sound/K6Fifth.lean) for open338,
readsOpen_full, rowsApart_full and the step from the rule's open set to the list: THAT FILE STANDS
ON EIGHT FILES OF THE OUTPUT HEAD's OWN CHAIN, WHICH THIS ONE DOES NOT NEED: hence the two tests are
evaluated here and the step is composed in place from Desc/Sound/SpineList.lean.

-/
